Q('rpsa','TARA','Problem Solving','Ordering','Five people stand in a line. A is before B and C is before D. Which must be true?',['A is first','D is not first','B is last','C is before A'],1,'D cannot be first because C must appear before D.'),
Q('rpsb','TARA','Problem Solving','Data','A shop reduces a £80 item by 25%, then increases the sale price by 10%. What is the final price?',['£60','£64','£66','£68'],2,'The sale price is £60, then 110% of £60 is £66.'),
Q('rpsc','TARA','Problem Solving','Spatial reasoning','A cube has opposite face pairs (1,6), (2,5), and (3,4). Which face is opposite 5?',['1','2','3','4'],1,'The stated pair containing 5 is (2,5).'),
Q('rpsd','TARA','Problem Solving','Rates','Three machines make 180 parts in 4 hours. How many parts do five machines make in 6 hours at the same rate?',['360','400','450','540'],2,'Each machine makes 15 parts per hour; 5×6×15=450.')
